# Dataset

## Source
This project uses the **UCDavis QUIC Network Traffic Dataset**  
Available on Kaggle: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/guillaumefraysse/ucdavisquic

## About the Dataset
- **Protocol:** QUIC (the transport layer behind HTTP/3)
- **Total Packets:** 344,539
- **Captured from:** Real Google service traffic

## Traffic Classes
| Class ID | Service | Traffic Type |
|----------|---------|--------------|
| 0 | Google Drive | File transfer / bulk upload |
| 1 | Google Docs | Real-time collaboration |
| 2 | Google Music | Audio streaming |
| 3 | Google Search | Web browsing |
| 4 | YouTube | Video streaming |

## Features
| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| timestamp | Unix timestamp of packet capture |
| time_delta | Time gap since previous packet (seconds) |
| packet_size | Size of packet in bytes |
| direction | 0 = inbound, 1 = outbound |
| Type | Traffic class label (target variable) |

## Why This Dataset?
QUIC is an encrypted protocol — traditional Deep Packet Inspection
cannot classify it by reading payload content.
This makes it a perfect use case for ML-based classification
using only flow-level features (size, timing).

## How to Download
The notebook automatically downloads the dataset using kagglehub:
​```python
import kagglehub
path = kagglehub.dataset_download("guillaumefraysse/ucdavisquic")
​```
No manual download needed.
